{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"View ▸ Show Hidden Files needed Finder's shortcut, ⇧⌘. (Command-Shift-period). The question was how to write it as an ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSMenuItem","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" key equivalent. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSEvent.charactersIgnoringModifiers","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" keeps the effect of Shift, so on a US layout the keystroke reports ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":">","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". That raised the worry that an item defined as ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"\".\"","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".shift","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in its mask would never match, and that it had to be ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"\">\"","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".command","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" instead.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The first probe seemed to confirm the worry, and it was wrong. It built the event by hand: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSEvent.keyEvent(with: .keyDown, ..., modifierFlags: [.command, .shift], characters: \">\", charactersIgnoringModifiers: \">\", keyCode: 47)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" sent to ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSMenu.performKeyEquivalent(with:)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" fired the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"\">\"","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" + ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".command","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" item and missed the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"\".\"","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" + ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"[.command, .shift]","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" item. A second hand-built event with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"\".\"","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in both character fields fired the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"\".\"","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" + shift item instead. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSEvent.keyEvent(with:...)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" takes the characters as arguments and does not derive them from the key code and the keyboard layout, so each probe only restated the characters its author guessed.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The repo forbids launching the app to verify a change, so the question had to be answered headless.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
