{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"A hand-built event makes a wrong definition look correct and a correct one look broken. The first probe here pointed at rewriting the committed ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"\".\"","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" + shift item as ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"\">\"","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" + ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".command","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", which would have shown ⌘> in the menu instead of ⇧⌘., the keystroke Finder uses.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
